  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive). Intransitive pair: {織|お}れる (can be woven - potential). Pattern: Xを{織|お}る (to weave X).\n\nASPECT: ている indicates ongoing action. {織|お}っている = 'is weaving.'\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {布|ぬの}を{織|お}る (to weave cloth)\n- {糸|いと}を{織|お}る (to weave thread)\n- {機|はた}で{織|お}る (to weave on a loom)\n\nCOMMON COMPOUNDS:\n- {手|て}{織|お}り (hand-woven)\n- {機|はた}{織|お}り (weaving, loom work)\n- {織物|おりもの} (woven fabric, textile)\n\nCULTURAL NOTE: Weaving has a long tradition in Japan, particularly for kimono fabrics like {西陣織|にしじんおり} (Nishijin weaving).",
